      "shortest": true,
      "solution": "s = input()\nr = 0\nfor i, c in enumerate(s):\n    if i <= r and c != '.':\n        r = max(r, i + int(c))\nprint(sum(c != '.' for c in s[r+1:]))",
      "statement": "Your little brother spent all afternoon lining up dominoes, and now it's time for the big push!\n\nThe row is described by a string [[S]]. Each . is an empty cell, and each digit [[h]] is a domino of height [[h]].\n\nYou push the first domino to the right. A falling domino of height [[h]] at position [[i]] hits every cell from [[i]] + 1 to [[i]] + [[h]], and every domino it hits falls too, continuing the chain.\n\nHow many dominoes are <<still standing>> at the end?\n\nExample: 2.1..3.1\nThe domino at position 0 (height 2) hits cells 1 and 2, knocking down the domino at position 2. That one (height 1) only reaches cell 3, which is empty, so the chain stops. The dominoes at positions 5 and 7 stay standing, so the answer is 2.",
